   "tuning": [],
   "is_new": true,
   "source": {
    "label": null,
    "number": "Theorem 1.6",
    "quote": "Let (ν, F) be a stationary, unstructured bandit, ρ a risk measure and π a policy. Assume that: (i) ρ is confusable over F ... (ii) π is strongly consistent over F ... Then ... lim inf E[N_T^k]/log T ⩾ 1/K_inf^{Fk,ρ}(νk; ρ⋆(ν)) ... In particular, the expected pseudo regret satisfies ... ⩾ Σ ∆k/K_inf(νk; ρ⋆(ν))."
   },
   "confidence": "medium",
   "notes": "Generalisation of Lai-Robbins/Burnetas-Katehakis to generic risk measures; Kinf is defined w.r.t. risk measure rho rather than mean. Also gives per-arm pull count lower bound."
  },
